From e920a39ece816eb7deb82f5b39123a45d93503e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 22 Feb 2026 13:49:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Unihertz 8849 hardware controls

Add a settings menu for the Unihertz 8849 (Tank) device-specific
hardware, detected via the Agold HAL and FPGA sysfs interface.

Features:
- Warning light with red/blue/green modes (ioctl 310)
- Camping light with off/full/medium/low/flash/SOS modes (ioctl 301)
- Projector enable/disable with sleep/wake FPGA init sequence (ioctl 500)
- Projector mode selection (portrait, landscape, landscape inverted)
- Phone display toggle while projecting
- Projector brightness, keystone correction, fan speed
- Focus calibration via motor sweep (focus_auto_calibration sysfs)
- Manual focus adjustment via motor_turn_mode_step
- Projector temperature and laser rangefinder readout
- Display viewport shrinks to 16:9 when projector is active to
  prevent clipping the projected image

The focus calibration button runs a per-device motor sweep, parses
the results from dmesg (init_cali_buff), and saves them as the
calibration table for the Agold daemon's continuous auto focus.
